@startuml
title Owner identity login and logout — v4

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor Owner
boundary "Browser SPA" as Browser
control "FERTO Worker" as Worker
database "D1" as D1
participant "Spotify Accounts" as Accounts
participant "Spotify Web API" as Spotify

== Sign in (identity only) ==

Owner -> Browser: Click "Sign in"
Browser -> Browser: Read ferto_csrf cookie
Browser -> Worker: POST /api/owner/login\nOrigin + X-CSRF-Token
Worker -> Worker: Validate same-origin and CSRF token

Worker -> Worker: Generate OAuth state + PKCE verifier (S256)
Worker -> D1: Delete expired oauth_states
Worker -> D1: Store hashed state, verifier, expiry
Worker --> Browser: { authorizeUrl }

Browser -> Accounts: Navigate authorizeUrl\nscope=user-read-private only
Owner -> Accounts: Approve identity sign-in
Accounts --> Browser: 302 APP_ORIGIN/api/owner/callback\ncode + state
Browser -> Worker: GET /api/owner/callback?code&state\n(navigational request)

Worker -> D1: Load unexpired verifier by hashed state
Worker -> D1: Delete the one-time oauth state

alt State missing or expired
  Worker --> Browser: 400 expired OAuth state
else State is valid
  Worker -> Accounts: Exchange code + PKCE verifier for tokens\n(no client secret)
  Accounts --> Worker: Short-lived access token
  Worker -> Spotify: GET /v1/me
  Spotify --> Worker: Profile (immutable account_id)

  alt Profile account_id is not OWNER_SPOTIFY_ID
    Worker --> Browser: 403 wrong Spotify account
  else Configured owner
    Worker -> Worker: Generate opaque session token
    Worker -> D1: Store HMAC(session token), owner account_id, expiry
    Worker --> Browser: 302 /?owner=1\nHttpOnly, SameSite=Lax session cookie (7 days)
    Browser --> Owner: Owner controls visible\n(Like / Never, refresh status)
  end
end

note over Worker,Browser #D9EAD3
  The browser never receives a Spotify credential: the
  access token lives only inside the Worker for this one
  callback exchange. The cookie it receives is a FERTO
  session cookie. This identity login is separate from
  the service token that rebuilds the catalogue.
end note

== Sign out ==

Owner -> Browser: Click "Logout"
Browser -> Worker: POST /api/owner/logout\nOrigin + X-CSRF-Token + session cookie
Worker -> Worker: Validate same-origin, CSRF, and owner session
Worker -> D1: Delete the owner_sessions row
Worker --> Browser: 200; clear session cookie
Browser --> Owner: Public read-only visitor view

@enduml
